Platform: aggregated App Store customer reviews / JustUseApp
Date: source published 2026-06-15; individual review dates not consistently
exposed
Customer language: One reviewer says the update =E2=80=9Ccompletely ruined=
=E2=80=9D the app
after custom voice functionality was replaced by canned voices, explaining
that they had created characters people identified with. Another explicitly
asks for more voice options to =E2=80=9Cbetter represent our pet babies.=E2=
=80=9D A further
review praises separate speed and pitch controls.
Wanted/problem: Users do not merely want any funny synthetic voice. They
build a stable imagined voice/persona for a specific pet and notice when it
changes. They want controllable pitch/speed, broader age/gender/personality
choices, and persistence across videos.
Current workaround/product: My Talking Pet; users manually tune recorded
voice pitch/speed or rely on preset voices.
Roast.pet implication: Treat VOICE as a locked identity attribute alongside
face/markings/personality. After likeness approval, preview 3 voice
candidates or simple controls (e.g. deep=E2=86=94high, slow=E2=86=94fast, d=
ry=E2=86=94excited), ask
=E2=80=9CWhich sounds most like them?=E2=80=9D, then persist the approved v=
oice for every
future roast/card/video for that pet.
Occasion/audience: repeat pet owners, birthday greetings, social sharing,
creator/fundraising characters, recurring family jokes.
Independent support: HIGH. MWM=E2=80=99s current My Talking Pet review summ=
ary says
voice pitch/speed problems are the most-mentioned negative issue (13
mentions), while its App Store description explicitly markets changing
voice from big dog to little cat. App Store customer evidence also says
pitch/speed control is valuable.
Confidence: HIGH
Prototype/test: Add a post-likeness step: =E2=80=9CPick their voice=E2=80=
=9D with 3 instant
audio samples =E2=80=94 Little menace / Normal chaos / Deep authority =E2=
=80=94 plus
optional Advanced pitch/speed sliders. Save selection to pet profile. A/B
test against one automatically selected voice on completion rate,
regenerate rate, and gift-recipient reaction.
Verdict: BUILD/TEST

Supporting sources:

   - https://mwm.ai/apps/my-talking-pet/1427290424
   - https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/my-talking-pet/id1427290424

STATE / CLUSTER UPDATE
Voice/personality identity: materially strengthened. This is distinct from
the already-established mouth-motion/animation correction cluster: the
visual animation can be technically good while the pet still feels wrong
because its voice has changed.

TOP 5 CUSTOMER REQUESTS TO PRODUCTIZE

   1. Exact pet identity approval before final generation =E2=80=94 face, m=
arkings,
   accessories and motion continuity.
   2. Personality-driven comedy =E2=80=94 pet quirks determine the roast pr=
emise
   and wording.
   3. Multi-pet compositions from separate photos, with each pet
   independently approved.
   4. Fast/last-minute digital gifting with clear ETA and deferred-photo
   surprise mode.
   5. NEWLY STRENGTHENED: selectable, persistent pet voice identity with
   preview and lightweight pitch/speed control.

STRONGEST UNMET NEED
A personalized funny gift where the animal remains recognizably the
recipient=E2=80=99s exact pet across appearance, motion, personality AND vo=
ice =E2=80=94
rather than becoming a generic talking dog/cat after animation.

EASIEST CONVERSION-LIFT CHANGE TO ORDERING FLOW
Immediately after identity approval, play three 2=E2=80=933 second voice sa=
mples
over the same line and ask: =E2=80=9CWhich sounds most like them?=E2=80=9D =
Save the answer.
This is cheap relative to rendering full video and reduces expensive
post-render voice rejection.

BEST NEW ETSY LISTING/PRODUCT IDEA FROM CUSTOMER LANGUAGE
=E2=80=9CYour Dog Roasts Dad =E2=80=94 Choose Their Voice =E2=80=94 Persona=
lized Talking Pet
Birthday Video + QR Card.=E2=80=9D Listing media should demonstrate the sam=
e pet in
three clearly different voices and make =E2=80=9CYOU PICK THEIR VOICE=E2=80=
=9D a visible
benefit.

IMPORTANT NEGATIVE SIGNAL
Do not rely on a single automatically chosen/canned AI voice. Existing
talking-pet users explicitly report that replacing their controllable
established voice with canned voices destroyed characters their audiences
recognized. Voice novelty is not enough; continuity matters for
personalization.

SEARCH NOTE
This run reviewed fresh web results across personalized-pet portrait/gift
sellers, Etsy last-minute portrait listings, talking-pet App Store/review
